From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orchard migration <noreply@orchardlinux>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:34:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] wifi: brcmfmac: Don't cancel reset work that was never
 initialized

brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work() runs from removal paths, including a
firmware request that fails before brcmf_attach() has initialized
drvr->bus_reset. Cancelling the uninitialized work item trips debug
object and lockdep checks.

Check bus_reset.func like brcmf_bus_schedule_reset() already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index dad6f4563..0f121ebbc 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -1184,7 +1184,7 @@ void brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work(struct brcmf_bus *bus_if)
 {
 	mutex_lock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 	bus_if->removing = true;
-	if (bus_if->drvr)
+	if (bus_if->drvr && bus_if->drvr->bus_reset.func)
 		cancel_work_sync(&bus_if->drvr->bus_reset);
 	mutex_unlock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 }
